From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: do not SPI-drain during probe read_message retry

v016 added syna_tcm_spi_drain_locked() to read_message retry paths (bad
marker / bad padding). On cold boot sensor_detection the first read often
shows marker 0x00 (RomBoot). Draining before the stock usleep+retry shifts
the bus and the second read returns report 0x03 → Failed to detect the
sensor. IRQ never registers.

Keep SPI drain only after probe: ISR failed read, ENABLE_REPORT timeout,
GET_TOUCH_REPORT_CONFIG retry. Remove drain from read_message retry.

Applies after syna-tcm-first-appinfo-resync.patch.

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
@@ -888,7 +888,6 @@ retry:
 		UNLOCK_BUFFER(tcm_hcd->in);
 		retval = -ENXIO;
 		if (retry) {
-			syna_tcm_spi_drain_locked(tcm_hcd);
 			usleep_range(READ_RETRY_US_MIN, READ_RETRY_US_MAX);
 			retry = false;
 			goto retry;
@@ -975,7 +974,6 @@ check_padding:
 			"Incorrect message padding byte (0x%02x)\n", tcm_hcd->in.buf[total_length - 1]);
 		UNLOCK_BUFFER(tcm_hcd->in);
 		if (retry) {
-			syna_tcm_spi_drain_locked(tcm_hcd);
 			usleep_range(READ_RETRY_US_MIN, READ_RETRY_US_MAX);
 			retry = false;
 			goto retry;
